Z||000000||fiero56||10-27-2001||05:48 PM||||I'm getting really excited. The new Nissan Altima is out. What a sweet looking design. 245hp available. I'd love to get my hads on one of those. <BR>The new Pontiac Vibe GT-r is due out in a few months. I would love to have one of those, even if they aren't much of a screamer in stock form, that will change with TRD making parts for the Matrix. 13" brakes in front, 19" wheels, 6-speed, etc, and I love the colors used in the interior. I wonder how much will make it to the showroom even with the top options.<P>Then there's the WRX, the new(er) Celica, and others. Lots of new exciting toys coming onto the market. I've been really tempted to check some of these out and maybe ditch one of the Fieros. Then I think of carpayments, and insurance, and I decide a really small Fiero isn't so bad. <P>I don't need a new car, I don't need a new car...||||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||10-27-2001||06:58 PM|||| Over the last few weeks I've been looking around, too. I think I'm at the point in my life where having a good ,reliable, normal car is important. So far I've looked at a Mazda MP5 (wanted a MP3 but they only got 2, sold'em both and Mazda isn't building anymore), a Hyundai Elantra GT(ugly), and a Sentra. I just can't justify the Stealth's bad gas milage and fragile drivetrain, and as I said, I want reliability, so the Fiero has a spot reserved under a cover in the garage. I recently left my spousal equivalent, got a new job(starts next week), and need to find a place to live. Performance cars just aren't that important anymore. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||10-27-2001||07:44 PM||||I can't wait for the new Z car and the RX-8; they will be kinda pricey, I'm sure, but they both look sweet and are quick <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  There are a lot of up and coming cars, in my opinion, just have to sit tight.  My personal favorite up and coming car is the new BMW Mini Cooper S, the sport version of the new Mini.  It has a lot to offer, and I love the looks, small car with big room, and interior design.  That car will almost surely be the first new car I buy (wait a few years till I'm graduated and it's not the first model year...never buy first model year).<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||10-27-2001||11:52 PM||||There sure are a lot of great new cars on the market.  I really like the new Acura RSX Type-S in particular.  I know some have criticized its styling as too bland, but I see it as a clean design thats sporty.  I don't like alll the lines and creases of the Celica GT-S from the side (head on it looks great IMO).  The Acura just seems more sleek with the styling comming together as a whole.  I don't think you can go wrong with a WRX.  All Wheel drive, a 227 HP turbo four, its a perfect performance car for snowy Buffalo.<P>I also cannot wait to see the new Z and RX-8.  As compacts, I think the 175 HP Nissan Sentra SE-R and 180 HP Focus SVT deserve mention too!  My only complaint with the upcoming Vibe is AWD is offered, but not with the 180 HP motor!  Come on GM (and Toyota) give us both in one car!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||10-28-2001||11:21 AM||||I will have to say that Pontiac/GM did better with the Vibe. Looks <I>much</I> better than the Aztek from every angle. I would probably buy one if I had the money. They're pretty cool.<P>I also love the Acura RSX. That's a car I would definately consider buying.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||14
